# lez-allowlist for the allocator: one LEZ account id per line, as reported by
# the tester's `lez_sign_module.account_id` (the base58 form, or the 64-hex
# form; the verifier decodes both to the same 32 bytes). Lines starting with #
# and blank lines are ignored; other lines are dropped and logged. Each account
# id is granted ONE membership (it is the vector's nullifier). Saving this file
# re-`serve`s the running allocator within ~30 s — no restart needed.
